# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Darkwhisper Gorge and Winterfall Village

step Darkwhisper Gorge
  tip Ride east, then south down Frostwhisper Gorge. The Frostmaul giants there are elite level 59: keep to the middle and keep moving. The strange source is at the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge, at the south end.
  goto 59.8,74.2 "Darkwhisper Gorge"
  complete 4842

step Level 59.9
  zone Winterspring
  when level<59.9
  tip Top up here to level 59.9 before the hand-ins at Winterspring: they take you to level 60. The Rabid Shardtooths (59) of Frostwhisper Gorge, just north of the strange source, give far more experience than the furbolgs by Timbermaw Hold. Or, with a group, run the Scholomance dungeon or the Stratholme dungeon instead.
  goto 60.1,71.2 map 1452 "Rabid Shardtooth"
  level 59.9 grind 7446               -- grind on Rabid Shardtooth

step Donova Snowden
  tip Ride back west to Frostfire Hot Springs.
  turnin 4842
  turnin 5087                         -- Donova Snowden
  note Donova next sends you after High Chief Winterfall, an elite in his cave. Skip it.

step Are We There, Yeti?
  kill 10978 quest 5163.1 @61.5,38.6 map 1452 "Scare Legacki with Umi's Mechanical Yeti"

step Everlook
  tip Ride east along the road to Everlook.
  turnin 5163                         -- Umi Rumplesnicker

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Level 60

step Dungeon instead of grinding
  tip Optional. Running Stratholme, Scholomance, Lower Blackrock Spire or Blackrock Depths with a group instead of grinding gets you there faster.
  note Optional: with a group, a 55-60 dungeon replaces the grind below.

step Grind to 60
  tip The quests run out here. Rabid Shardtooths prowl Frostwhisper Gorge in southern Winterspring, south of the road from Everlook.
  goto 60.1,71.2 "Frostwhisper Gorge"
  level 60 grind 7446 -- grind on Rabid Shardtooth at Frostwhisper Gorge, Winterspring
  train class optional only Warrior,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Shaman,Mage,Warlock -- In Orgrimmar: fly from Everlook
  train class optional only Druid,Paladin -- In Thunder Bluff: fly from Everlook
